# Copy to deploy/pi/.env (gitignored) — read by deploy/k3s/make-secrets.sh
# (and by the superseded deploy/pi/docker-compose.yml).
#
# This file configures the CONTAINERS. The application's own settings stay in
# the repo-root .env (CC_* vars). Two files, two audiences; don't merge them.
#
# Every variable below is marked:
#   GENERATED — you invent it once; nothing outside this file knows the value.
#               `./deploy/k3s/init-env.sh` fills every empty one for you
#               (`openssl rand -hex 32`) and never overwrites a value that is
#               already set. Do it by hand only if you have a reason.
#   ELICITED  — it comes from somewhere outside: an upstream endpoint, a
#               provider, a minted LiteLLM virtual key, an existing dump.
#
# On a RESTORE, a value marked GENERATED that already exists must be COPIED,
# not regenerated — see the never-rotate warning under LiteLLM and n8n.
# On a FULLY-CLEAN deployment (nothing retained), generate all of them fresh
# and accept that everything encrypted under the old keys is gone.

# --- Knowledge graph (neo4j + graphiti) ---
# GENERATED (`openssl rand -hex 32`). On a restore it must match the dumped
# Neo4j store, or auth fails after the load.
NEO4J_PASSWORD=

# --- Graphiti's three model credentials (all LOCAL since 2026-08-01) ---
# ELICITED — all three are LiteLLM VIRTUAL KEYS minted against the running
# proxy, each scoped to one model group so a leak in one cannot spend through
# another:
#   GRAPHITI_LLM_API_KEY -> ["graphiti-llm"]              entity extraction
#   EMBEDDER_API_KEY     -> ["qwen3-embedding-local"]     embeddings
#   RERANKER_API_KEY     -> ["cc-default","qwen3-rerank-local"] cross-encoder
# (that last scope said `gpt-4.1-nano` until 2026-08-23 — stale since the
# 2026-08-19 true-cross-encoder switch; the live key has always matched the
# corrected list, so this comment was the only thing wrong.)
#
# Mint them with `./deploy/k3s/mint-keys.sh`, which does exactly this against
# the running proxy and writes the results back here.
# CHICKEN-AND-EGG on a fully-clean deployment: the proxy must be up before
# these can exist, and the proxy needs a Secret before it can start.
# `./deploy/k3s/init-env.sh` writes the literal PENDING into all three to break
# the cycle — make-secrets.sh accepts PENDING (it refuses only EMPTY), the
# trio comes up, then mint-keys.sh replaces them, re-runs make-secrets.sh and
# restarts graphiti.
#
# `graphiti-llm` must stay registered as openai/chat_completions/<model>: the
# prefix forces LiteLLM's Responses->chat-completions bridge, without which
# graphiti's structured extraction silently receives prose. See the long note
# in deploy/pi/graphiti/config.yaml.
GRAPHITI_LLM_API_KEY=
EMBEDDER_API_KEY=
RERANKER_API_KEY=
# ELICITED, both OPTIONAL (empty is fine and is today's state). Passed into the
# litellm container for DB-registered models that route to those providers.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately absent — its absence is what makes Claude
# Code's /anthropic passthrough use the subscription. Read the note in
# deploy/pi/litellm/config.yaml before adding any Anthropic credential.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- LiteLLM ---
# GENERATED, all three (`openssl rand -hex 32`; the master key is conventionally
# `sk-` + random, and anything works).
#
# !! NEVER ROTATE LITELLM_SALT_KEY !! It encrypts the stored virtual keys and
# provider credentials in cc-litellm-db. A fresh salt over an existing database
# leaves the rows present and undecryptable. On a restore, COPY the old value.
#
# A fresh LITELLM_MASTER_KEY is a fresh admin credential: every downstream
# virtual key (the three above, plus the app's CC_LLM_API_KEY in the root .env)
# must be re-minted against it.
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
LITELLM_SALT_KEY=
LITELLM_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# ELICITED, optional — compose-only (the k3s manifests do not read it). Only
# relevant if a DB-registered model routes to a local Ollama.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# --- n8n (the email facade — it holds the Gmail OAuth) ---
# GENERATED: N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY (`openssl rand -hex 32`) and N8N_DB_PASSWORD.
#
# !! NEVER ROTATE N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY !! It decrypts the stored Gmail
# credential. Restoring an n8n dump under a different value leaves the
# credential row present, undecryptable, and the mail feed dies silently. On a
# restore, COPY the old value; on a fully-clean deployment, generate a new one
# and expect to re-create the Gmail credential (or import it decrypted — see
# the /setup skill's phase 3).
N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
N8N_DB_PASSWORD=
# ELICITED, all defaulted — make-secrets.sh substitutes these exact values when
# blank, so leaving them is fine on a single-host install.
N8N_DB_USER=n8n
N8N_DB_NAME=n8n
N8N_HOST=localhost
N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=http://localhost:5678/

# ELICITED, defaulted to UTC by make-secrets.sh if blank.
TIMEZONE=America/Chicago

# --- cc-crawler's OPTIONAL LLM mode ---
# ELICITED, both optional. make-secrets.sh creates secret/cc-crawler-llm only
# when CC_LLM_API_KEY is set — and it reads that one from the REPO-ROOT .env,
# deliberately, rather than duplicating the credential here. Without the
# secret the crawler still runs, pruning heuristically. These two only override
# the defaults (http://litellm:4000/v1 and cc-default).
#CC_CRAWLER_LLM_BASE_URL=http://litellm:4000/v1
#CC_CRAWLER_LLM_MODEL=cc-default

# --- topology (2026-08-27 role-label contract) ---
# ELICITED, defaulted to today's homelab. The manifests place workloads by the
# node labels cc-role/anchor (small stateful stores, control plane) and
# cc-role/compute (JVM/gVisor/Chromium muscle) — label the nodes once:
#   kubectl label node <anchor>  cc-role/anchor=true
#   kubectl label node <compute> cc-role/compute=true
# CC_COMPUTE_SSH is the passwordless ssh target for the compute node; every
# build script, install-gvisor.sh and verify.sh read it (default:
# chromebox_admin@100.113.118.28).
#CC_COMPUTE_SSH=chromebox_admin@100.113.118.28
